---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../lib/site';
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="How AdMobot collects, uses and protects your data." updated="12 October 2026">
  <p>
    This policy explains what information {SITE.legalName} ("AdMobot", "we"), the business that builds and runs AdMobot, collects when you use our website and the AdMobot app, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We follow India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your email address and a securely hashed password, and the name of your workspace.</li>
    <li><strong>Brand information you give us:</strong> your website address and what we read from your public website, your Brand Brain (voice, audience, products, offers, notes), uploaded images, and the posts you create, edit or approve.</li>
    <li><strong>Connected channels:</strong> when you connect Instagram, Facebook, Threads, LinkedIn, X, Pinterest, Google Business Profile or another channel, we store the access token that platform gives us, the account or Page name, and the IDs of posts we publish for you. We read the engagement numbers (likes, comments, shares, saves, reach) of those posts and, if you use the Inbox, the comments people leave on your posts.</li>
    <li><strong>Your ad and analytics accounts:</strong> if you connect your Meta Ads, Google Ads, Google Analytics or Search Console accounts, we store the access token, the account names and IDs, and the campaign, ad and performance data we read from them to launch and report on campaigns you approved.</li>
    <li><strong>Store catalogue:</strong> if you connect a Shopify store, the public product names, prices, images and availability.</li>
    <li><strong>Early-access requests:</strong> the email address you enter, the page you signed up from and campaign tags in the link you followed.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing:</strong> when paid plans start, payments are handled by Cashfree Payments (rupee payments in India) and Razorpay (international card payments in US dollars), or by bank transfer. We receive the status of your payment, not your full card or UPI details.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> basic server logs (IP address, browser, time of request) kept for security and troubleshooting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the service: learn your brand, plan and write content, create images, publish to the channels you connected, and show you how posts performed.</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure and working, and to answer your support requests.</li>
    <li>To email you about your account, your trial and important changes. Marketing emails only if you opted in, with an unsubscribe link in each.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use your private content to advertise to you.</p>

  <h2>AI processing</h2>
  <p>
    To write content and analyse your brand, relevant parts of your brand information, and the text of comments or reviews you ask AdMobot to answer, are sent to our AI provider, Google, through the Gemini API, and processed under Google's API terms. We send only what is needed for the task. We do not use data we receive from Google, Meta or the other platforms to develop, improve or train AI or machine-learning models.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>We use trusted providers to run AdMobot. They process data only on our instructions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Supabase — database and sign-in (servers in Singapore)</li>
    <li>Render — application hosting (Singapore)</li>
    <li>Cloudflare — the app's front end and file storage; GitHub Pages — website hosting</li>
    <li>Our email delivery provider (Amazon SES or Resend) — to send the emails you ask AdMobot to send and our account emails</li>
    <li>Google — AI processing (Gemini API)</li>
    <li>Meta, LinkedIn, X and the other channels you connect — to publish your posts and read their metrics</li>
    <li>Cashfree Payments and Razorpay — payments</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data from Meta, Threads, LinkedIn, X and Pinterest</h2>
  <p>
    We use data from these platforms, and from the Meta ad account you connect, only to publish the content you approve, to launch and manage the ads you approve, and to show you how they performed. We do not sell it, share it with third parties for advertising, or use it for any other purpose. You can disconnect a channel at any time in the app, which deletes its access token from our servers, and you can revoke AdMobot's access from the platform's own settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Data from Google</h2>
  <p>
    If you connect Google Business Profile, Google Analytics, Google Search Console, Google Ads or YouTube, AdMobot receives data from Google APIs with the access you grant on Google's consent screen:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Business Profile:</strong> your business accounts and locations, so you can pick one, and the local posts we publish there for you.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics and Search Console (read-only):</strong> your analytics properties and Search Console sites, and reports on sessions, conversions, search queries, clicks and impressions, shown only to you in your Analytics screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Ads:</strong> the ad accounts you can access, so you can pick one, and the campaigns, budgets, ads and daily results we create, change and read after you approve them. Your own payment profile pays Google; we never hold your ad money.</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube (only if you turn it on):</strong> uploading the videos you attach to a post you approved.</li>
    <li><strong>Your Google account email</strong>, to show you which account is connected.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    AdMobot's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. We use this data only to provide and improve these user-facing features. We do not use it for advertising, do not sell it, do not transfer it to others except as needed to provide the features, to comply with law, or as part of a merger, and our people do not read it except with your consent, for security, or where the law requires. You can disconnect any Google service in AdMobot, which deletes the stored tokens, and revoke access at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your workspace while your account is active. If you delete your account or ask us to, we delete your workspace, content, images and tokens within 30 days, except where the law requires us to keep billing records.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can access, correct or delete your data, withdraw consent and nominate someone to exercise your rights. Most of this you can do in the app; for anything else, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. See also <a href={url('/data-deletion')}>how to delete your data</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The website uses no advertising cookies. It uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people find useful; Google Analytics sets its own cookies (named <code>_ga</code>) and receives your IP address, browser and the pages you view. We don't use it for advertising or to identify you. You can block it with your browser's privacy settings or the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>. The app uses essential storage to keep you signed in and no analytics.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). Channel tokens stay on our servers and are never sent to your browser. Access to production systems is limited to the people who run the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>AdMobot is a business tool and is not meant for anyone under 18.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy we will update the date above, and tell you by email for significant changes. Questions or complaints: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> ({SITE.legalName}, {SITE.country}).
  </p>
</Legal>
